# Hub governance: bylaws + proposals

Spec: `docs/modules/BYLAWS_PROPOSALS.md`. Read before touching these paths.

## Model

- **Public tools stay on-device.** `HubDraftSyncPanel` appears only for a
  signed-in officer (module enabled, write role, has a local). Sync POSTs the
  current draft as a new Hub record — never a live two-way bind.
- Bylaw drafts: `bylaw_drafts` with `form` jsonb (builder values). Status
  lifecycle `draft → committee → pending_gmm → adopted / archived`. Preview is
  regenerated from the stored form with the same builder lib (`build-template`).
- Proposal packages: rows (article / current language / union proposal /
  employer counter / status / notes / assignees), confidential `caucus_note`,
  `proposal_events` timeline, `proposal_publications` member-safe snapshots.

## Tenancy

- Every table carries `union_id`/`local_id` + RLS (migration 0039).
- **RLS is route-wrapped, not auto-scoped.** Adapter method names
  (`listPackages`, `createPackage`, `upsertRow`, …) do not match the rls-store
  `list`/`create` keys, so every route wraps store calls in
  `withRlsContext(rlsContextForSession(session) ?? {}, ...)`. `withTenantRlsScope`
  would pass through silently.
- Cross-local (union/division/platform admin) lists union-wide when no local.

## Portal safety

- `/portal/proposals` returns publications only — never counters, caucus notes,
  or employer language. The route returns `{ publications: [] }` (or the page
  `notFound()`) when the union lacks the `proposals` module.
- Publish writes the publication first; `published_summary` on the package is a
  mirror. Archiving a publication hides it from the Portal.

## Copy guard

`hubBylaws`, `hubProposals`, `hubDraftSync`, `portalProposals` are Hub
namespaces (HUB_NS). No national union names; error strings carry a remedy.
EN/FR value parity, not just key parity.